        label: 'DANGER, Potentially lethal',
        title: 'MDMA + MAOIs',
        summary: 'This combination can cause fatal serotonin syndrome. MAOIs block monoamine oxidase, the enzyme that breaks down serotonin. MDMA simultaneously triggers a massive serotonin flood. The resulting overload is life-threatening. A documented 1987 case report describes severe agony and near-death; subsequent case series confirm multiple fatalities <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2884326/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="supp-link">[PMID 2884326]</a> <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9737504/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="supp-link">[PMID 9737504]</a>.',
        mechanism: 'MDMA floods serotonin transporters (SERT), causing massive synaptic serotonin release. MAOIs (irreversible: phenelzine, tranylcypromine; reversible: moclobemide) prevent enzymatic serotonin breakdown. Combined serotonin levels can reach lethal concentrations.',
