      [key('mdma','alcohol')]: {
        severity: 'moderate',
        label: 'CAUTION, Dehydration & cardiovascular strain',
        title: 'MDMA + Alcohol',
        summary: 'MDMA causes water retention (SIADH); alcohol causes dehydration. Both stress the cardiovascular system. Alcohol also blunts some MDMA effects while masking overdose warning signs.',
        mechanism: 'MDMA induces SIADH (syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone), causing fluid retention. Alcohol suppresses ADH, causing diuresis. The combination creates unpredictable fluid imbalance. Both independently elevate heart rate and body temperature.',
        advice: 'Limit alcohol to 1–2 drinks maximum if you choose to drink at all. Continue drinking 250–500ml of water per hour. Alcohol masks key MDMA overdose warning signs, be attentive to the people around you.',
