        summary: '"Greening out", nausea, sweating, pallor, dizziness, is significantly more likely when alcohol precedes cannabis. Alcohol increases intestinal THC absorption, leading to unexpectedly strong and unpleasant effects.',
        mechanism: 'Alcohol increases intestinal permeability and raises blood THC levels when taken before cannabis. The "crossfade" dramatically amplifies both subjective intoxication and nausea. The effect is especially pronounced with edibles.',
        advice: 'If combining, use cannabis first (or simultaneously) rather than alcohol first. Start with a very small cannabis amount. Eat beforehand. A greening out person should lie down in a safe position and will recover without medical treatment in most cases.',
        emergency: false
      },

      [key('alcohol','amphetamine')]: {
