        label: 'MODERATE, Masking & cardiovascular strain',
        title: 'Alcohol + Amphetamines',
        summary: 'Amphetamines mask alcohol intoxication, leading to excessive drinking. The combination strains the heart, causes severe dehydration, and dramatically worsens hangover. Alcohol toxicity accumulates silently.',
        mechanism: 'Stimulant-depressant masking: amphetamines reduce subjective drunkenness without reducing blood alcohol level or organ toxicity. Heart rate remains elevated as both substances exert competing effects.',
        advice: 'Track alcohol units explicitly when using stimulants, do not drink to "feel drunk." The liver still metabolizes the same amount of alcohol regardless of how drunk you feel. Rehydrate aggressively.',
