        summary: 'GHB\'s sedating effect competes with MDMA\'s stimulant properties, creating an unpredictable experience. The stimulant effects of MDMA can mask GHB-induced CNS depression, making it difficult to gauge intoxication depth and increasing overdose risk.',
        mechanism: 'MDMA\'s dopamine/norepinephrine stimulation partially masks GHB\'s sedation. As MDMA wears off, GHB\'s depressant effects can emerge rapidly and more intensely than expected.',
        advice: 'Use very small amounts of GHB if combining. Avoid redosing GHB, its half-life means doses stack rapidly. Have a sober person present.',
