        label: 'HIGH RISK, Serotonin syndrome',
        title: 'Tramadol + MDMA',
        summary: 'Tramadol has dual action: mu-opioid agonism plus serotonin/norepinephrine reuptake inhibition. Combined with MDMA\'s massive serotonin flood, the serotonergic load can cause serotonin syndrome. Multiple FAERS database cases of MDMA-associated serotonin syndrome involve opioid analgesics as cofactors <a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8820588/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="supp-link">[PMC8820588]</a>.',
        mechanism: 'Tramadol inhibits SERT and NET (serotonin/norepinephrine reuptake) while also acting as a weak mu-opioid agonist. The SERT inhibition directly adds to MDMA\'s serotonin release, raising serotonin syndrome risk in a dose-dependent way.',
        advice: 'Avoid combining. If tramadol is prescribed for pain, do not use MDMA on that day. Signs of serotonin syndrome (agitation, sweating, tremor, hyperthermia, rapid heartbeat) require emergency care.',
        emergency: false
      },
      [key('ssri','tramadol')]: {
        severity: 'caution',
        label: 'HIGH RISK, Serotonin syndrome (documented cases)',
        title: 'Tramadol + SSRIs / SNRIs',
        summary: 'Well-documented clinical interaction. Multiple case reports and FAERS data confirm serotonin syndrome from tramadol combined with SSRIs or SNRIs <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24153222/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="supp-link">[PMID 24153222]</a> <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23212934/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="supp-link">[PMID 23212934]</a>. Many people are prescribed both without adequate warning.',
        mechanism: 'Tramadol inhibits SERT (like SSRIs), creating overlapping serotonin reuptake inhibition. CYP2D6 inhibition by many SSRIs (especially fluoxetine, paroxetine) also slows tramadol metabolism, raising plasma levels unpredictably.',
        advice: 'If prescribed tramadol while on an SSRI, ask your doctor about the interaction explicitly. Do not increase tramadol dose without guidance. Serotonin syndrome symptoms require emergency care.',
        emergency: false
      },
      [key('maoi','tramadol')]: {
