        label: 'DANGER, Severe serotonin syndrome',
        title: 'Tramadol + MAOIs',
        summary: 'Potentially fatal combination. Tramadol\'s serotonin reuptake inhibition combined with MAOI-blocked serotonin breakdown can cause severe, rapidly-developing serotonin syndrome.',
        mechanism: 'Tramadol inhibits SERT while MAOIs block MAO-A/B, preventing serotonin metabolism. The combined serotonergic burden is similar to MDMA+MAOI in mechanism if not in magnitude.',
        advice: 'Do not combine. If taking an MAOI, tramadol is contraindicated. Use alternative analgesics (paracetamol/acetaminophen, ibuprofen) instead.',
        emergency: true
      },
      [key('tramadol','benzo')]: {
