        label: 'MODERATE, Respiratory depression & impaired judgment',
        title: 'Tramadol + Alcohol',
        summary: 'Alcohol adds CNS depression to tramadol\'s opioid effects, increasing sedation and respiratory depression risk. Seizure threshold is also lowered, tramadol already reduces seizure threshold.',
        mechanism: 'Tramadol\'s opioid and serotonergic effects combined with alcohol\'s GABA potentiation depress CNS function. Notably, tramadol itself can cause seizures at higher doses, alcohol further lowers this threshold.',
        advice: 'Avoid alcohol if taking tramadol. Do not drive or operate machinery. Seizure risk is real, if someone experiences a tramadol-related seizure, call emergency services.',
        emergency: false
