      [key('nicotine','mdma')]: {
        severity: 'moderate',
        label: 'MODERATE, Vasoconstriction worsens heat risk',
        title: 'Nicotine + MDMA',
        summary: 'One of the most common festival combinations. Both are cardiovascular stimulants. Nicotine adds peripheral vasoconstriction and heart rate elevation on top of MDMA\'s already significant cardiovascular burden — and vasoconstriction directly impairs the skin-based heat dissipation that prevents hyperthermia, MDMA\'s primary acute risk.',
        mechanism: 'Nicotine stimulates nicotinic acetylcholine receptors, releasing norepinephrine and dopamine. This compounds MDMA\'s monoamine release. Crucially, nicotine-induced peripheral vasoconstriction narrows skin blood vessels, reducing the body\'s ability to radiate heat outward — worsening MDMA\'s thermoregulatory impairment.',
        advice: 'Minimize smoking or vaping while dancing on MDMA. The vasoconstriction effect is worst during peak MDMA effects and physical exertion. Step off the floor, cool down, and rehydrate before and after any nicotine use.',
