        mechanism: 'Additive norepinephrine and dopamine release from both compounds compounds cardiovascular demand. Heart rate and blood pressure elevation is pharmacodynamically additive.',
        advice: 'If on prescription amphetamines and noticing elevated heart rate or blood pressure, reducing nicotine intake is the most accessible lever. Avoid smoking heavily during the peak of stimulant effect.',
        emergency: false
      },
      [key('nicotine','alcohol')]: {
        severity: 'low',
        label: 'LOW RISK, Minor interaction',
        title: 'Nicotine + Alcohol',
        summary: 'Very common combination. Alcohol mildly increases nicotine\'s rewarding effects through cross-sensitization of reward pathways — which is partly why the two co-occur so frequently. The physiological interaction is modest at typical doses.',
        mechanism: 'Alcohol enhances nicotinic acetylcholine receptor sensitivity in reward circuits, slightly increasing nicotine\'s subjective effects. Some evidence suggests alcohol mildly slows nicotine metabolism via CYP2A6 inhibition.',
        advice: 'Short-term interaction risk is low. The main concern is behavioral: heavy drinking tends to increase cigarette or vape consumption, which has its own respiratory and cardiovascular consequences over time.',
        emergency: false
      },
      [key('nicotine','cannabis')]: {
        severity: 'low',
        label: 'LOW RISK, Minor pharmacological interaction',
        title: 'Nicotine + Cannabis',
        summary: 'Commonly combined, particularly in countries where tobacco-cannabis mixtures are common. No significant pharmacokinetic interaction. The main harm concern is the tobacco combustion products, not the nicotine-cannabis pharmacology.',
        mechanism: 'Endocannabinoid system modulates nicotinic receptor sensitivity modestly. No significant pharmacokinetic interaction between the two compounds has been established.',
        advice: 'If smoking cannabis mixed with tobacco, the tobacco itself (not the nicotine-cannabis interaction) is the primary respiratory and addiction risk. Using a vaporizer eliminates combustion byproducts.',
        emergency: false
      },
      [key('nicotine','caffeine')]: {
        severity: 'low',
        label: 'LOW RISK, Mild additive stimulation',
        title: 'Nicotine + Caffeine',
        summary: 'Extremely common combination. Both are mild stimulants with cardiovascular effects. At typical doses the combination is well-tolerated. At very high doses of both — multiple energy drinks plus heavy nicotine use — cardiovascular burden becomes more meaningful.',
        mechanism: 'Caffeine blocks adenosine receptors (mild sympathomimetic). Nicotine stimulates catecholamine release. Combined cardiovascular stimulation — heart rate and blood pressure — is mildly additive.',
        advice: 'At typical daily use levels, risk is low. At very high combined doses (energy drinks + chain-vaping), be mindful of elevated heart rate and anxiety. Reduce one or both if feeling overstimulated.',
        emergency: false
      },
      [key('nicotine','maoi')]: {
